      "notes": "The page's Cabbage/Message rows carry their own citation: 'Only obtained if a player ends the raid with 0 individual contribution points.' The naive parser attaches no condition to these rows at all (they are DropsLineReward rows under an always-mode heading with no row-level marker the parser reads), so the generated document currently awards Cabbage and Message unconditionally on every single kill in addition to whatever else drops -- a real bug this override fixes, not merely an approximation. gemw=No on Message (Theatre of Blood) in the page's own template call, carried through as a display fact only; this model has no GE-value gating mechanism and doesn't need one here."
