      "notes": "P(unique) = tobPoints / (32 x urate), reducing to exactly 1/9.1 (Normal) or 1/7.7 (Hard/Hard-fast) at full points. 'hard-fast' is a second variant value (not a new SimContext field) for Hard Mode completed within the wiki's stated time bonus -- the unique roll itself is identical to plain 'hard' (same urate, same item weights), only tob:common's quantity multiplier differs (1.30 flat vs 1.15), which is why this table duplicates the 7-item pool across both hard-shaped entries rather than expressing the distinction once. Entry Mode gets no entry here at all -- 'Entry Mode grants no unique pre-roll at all', deterministically common-only, per the page's own prose (the calculator has no Entry option either, so nothing contradicts this). Gated on tobPoints>=1 explicitly even though the formula alone already returns exactly 0 in that state (evaluateFormula accepts 0), matching how the module treats zero points as a distinct branch rather than a degenerate probability."
    },
