      "notes": "3 rolls, denominator 30. Quantities are floor(item.min x modeMultiplier x ratio) to floor(that x 1.2), where ratio = tobPoints/32 (Normal/Hard/Hard-fast) and modeMultiplier is 1/1.15/1.30 by variant -- see tob_common_qty. Item minimums are Module:Theatre of Blood calculator's `normies` table, cross-checked item-by-item against the page's own rendered DropsLineReward rows: Death rune, Runite ore, Grimy torstol, Rune battleaxe/platebody/chainbody, Palm tree/Yew/Magic seed and Mahogany seed all match the module exactly (including three cases where the range collapses to one value, e.g. Yew seed's stated quantity of a bare 3). Vial of blood is the one exception: the page states 45-60, the module predicts 50-60 (floor(50x1.2)=60 matches the page's own high end; only the low end differs). Used the module's 50, not the page's 45 -- the page was re-fetched fresh this session (revid climbed from 15293917 to 15299363 on an unrelated capitalization edit) and the value was unchanged, ruling out simple staleness, and every other item's exact match against the module leaves the page's 45 looking like the one outlier rather than the module being wrong. Entries are gated on tobPoints>=1 for every variant including Entry, which is a defensive extrapolation for Entry specifically (the calculator has no Entry Mode option at all, so whether Entry's own -80% composes with a zero-points state is unconfirmed either way) -- chosen over letting Entry mode roll tiny near-zero quantities at the same extreme-deaths edge case Normal/Hard hit.",
