      "notes": "Tertiary rewards are independent of the unique/common outcome and always rolled (no tobPoints gate). All five items carry the page's own 'Drop rate scales down based on the individual's performance during the raid' disclaimer with no cited magnitude anywhere -- the fixed rates below are the best-available published figures, not a full model of that scaling, matching the same-shaped UNKNOWN this project already declines to guess for Duke Sucellus/Zalcano. Elite clue's per-variant split (Entry 1/25, Normal 3/25, Hard 3.5/25) is the page's own citation, not the template's bare 'rarity=1/25' field, which is Entry's rate only and would have been wrong for Normal/Hard if read literally -- exactly what the currently-generated document does. Holy ornament kit, Sanguine ornament kit and Sanguine dust are ALL Hard-Mode-only: all three reference the identical named {{refn|hardmode}} group, whose one defining occurrence (on Sanguine dust) reads 'Only obtainable in Hard Mode' -- a finding not previously recorded in this project's research, since the two ornament kits' own occurrences of the reference carry no visible text of their own. Lil' Zik's Entry-Mode rate is not stated anywhere on the page (only 'Normal Mode and Hard Mode' are named in the cited tweet); assumed equal to Normal's 1/650 as the more conservative reading, absent evidence of a third figure."
